Z||000000||Jay||12-30-2001||06:08 PM||||Okay, as many of you know I sold my N*  The new owner was driving it to L.A. yesterday when the car died in Utah.  He had it towed to a garage and they told him it was the fuel pump.  The new owner says he can hear the fuel pump prime and he has changed the filter.  Doing a fuel pressure test it shows 50psi and then when the key is turned it goes down to 40psi.  I can't remember what the psi should be at and can't find any notes.  Anyone know off hand?  That is all the info I was able to get, he was on a cell phone.  Thanks in advance.  I feel terrible.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||12-30-2001||06:37 PM||||I don't know much about the N* but, 40-50 PSI sounds about right.   I wonder if it could be something as easy as a fuse I hope.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||12-30-2001||09:52 PM||||After finding out more, I believe it is the ignition modual.  He's gonna let me know if there is spark.  It's not a fuse because he can hear the pump prime.||||reg||1
